WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.979
If you want to hear how a trap that never
came to fruition in a previous Saw movie makes

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.560
an appearance in Spiral, then stick around
to the end of this video.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.740
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.930
This is the first time we've ever gotten a
big establishing shot of the city, and it

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.310
looks like New York.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.680
Previous Saw films took place in a state called
The Fairweather State and the city name is

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.020
always just "Metropolitan", we never hear
the actual city name.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.160
There are definitely parts that look like
New York in the past, but it's hard to say

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.590
if that means the whole series takes place
there, or if this is simply a case of New

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.859
York playing the part of the fictional city.

00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:38.280
Another possibility is that this doesn't take
place in the same city as the other 8 films.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.320
If the new Jigsaw is someone who was inspired
by John Kramer, we could be anywhere in the

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.320
country now.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.559
The one big piece of evidence for that is
the fact that subway systems seem to be a

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:50.399
big part of the story here, possibly even
one of the traps involves the subway.

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:54.230
That reminds me of the trap we see in Jill
Tuck's dream in Saw 7, which involves a device

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.780
on a rail system, and interestingly enough,
has a Spiral thing going on.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.269
This obviously was never a real trap, but
Jill, who if you don't remember was John Kramer's

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:05.610
ex wife, had to get the idea from somewhere,
maybe this was an idea for a trap that John

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.210
never used and is being brought back by this
new killer.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.930
The movie is called Spiral, which is obviously
a reference to the pattern that shows up many

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:15.130
times throughout the Saw films, most notably
on Billy the Puppet.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.160
I wonder if we learn more about the thematic
meaning behind it.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.740
All of the images associated with Jigsaw were
chosen for a reason, and I'm guessing this

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:22.800
is no different.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.130
Just look at the spiral staircase in this
shot and the Spirals that cover the traps

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.300
across the trailer.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.820
Perhaps the reason for the Spiral symbol is
that it represents the religious aspect of

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.050
Jigsaw's following.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.840
John's work has always been kind of cult-like.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.820
He wears a robe and passes his teachings down
to his disciples.

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.740
The spiral symbol has a great contrast to
the symbols of popular religious icons, like

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:43.240
the cross, with its rigid, perpendicular edges.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.410
We see a Christian church appear in the trailer.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.030
The full title is Spiral: From The Book of
Saw.

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:51.820
Maybe the "book" is essentially a bible meant
to pass down the teachings of John Kramer.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.030
In fact, at the beginning of the trailer,
the character Detective Banks seems to be

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.880
imparting Jigsaw's code onto his partner,
whether it is intentionally or not.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.310
John's motto was "cherish your life", and
here's what Banks has to say about his partner's

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.950
relationship with his wife and son.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.380
"...Emma, this is my son Charlie."

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.600
"Enjoy it while it lasts."

00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:11.150
Kind of a weird thing to say.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.909
And I'm not saying that he's Jigsaw, mostly
just because that would be way too obvious.

00:02:14.909 --> 00:02:18.379
In the shot where a light is shined on this
figure underground, I noticed that the suspect

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:21.989
isn't actually moving, and that leads me to
believe that it could be a mannequin.

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:25.359
You may remember John's original workshop
was located in a mannequin factory.

00:02:25.359 --> 00:02:27.069
Also, take a look at the shadow.

00:02:27.069 --> 00:02:30.790
Based on the angle of the light, it should
be a long shadow, but it's not.

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:34.480
Meaning that this part must be a mural, which
may or may not be part of a trap.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.860
"It's a trap!"

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.450
You would love this franchise Admiral.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.920
Later in the trailer you can see a SWAT guy
cutting something with a buzzsaw.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.879
I think it would be really cool if the new
villain named himself Buzzsaw.

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:47.310
Also, it' looks like he's cutting away one
of those secret doors, like we saw in Gideon

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.200
Meatpacking Plant in Saw 5.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.200
The trap we do see just before the title card
hits looks to be a new take on an old classic,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.790
the good old reverse bear trap, only it looks
like the technology has been updated for 2020;

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.849
this one looks to be a hand-free version.

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:04.269
It does look as if this movie is pretty removed
from the last two entries, Saw 7 and Jigsaw.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:05.510
Here's something interesting to note.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.730
The seven Saw films all share a common look.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:10.319
The color schemes are similar and they use
the same aspect ratio.

00:03:10.319 --> 00:03:14.840
Spiral seems to have a similar aspect ratio
and look to the 2017 sequel Jigsaw, but as

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.739
far as we know, there are no Jigsaw characters
in Spiral.

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.069
All we know about the killer here is that
he's going after cops,

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:22.170
"They're targeting cops."

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.659
That could suggest that it's Logan Nelson,
from Jigsaw, whose goal was to get revenge

00:03:25.659 --> 00:03:29.540
on the corrupt cop who was responsible for
letting his wife's killer go free... but again...

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.959
it seems too obvious.

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:34.930
It feels as if this movie is setting up a
new Jigsaw successor, and maybe Spiral, is

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.260
part of a new trilogy or tetralogy, where
each movie introduces us to a new successor,

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.890
and in the final movie they end up battling
it out... or teaming up to make the ultimate

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:43.919
team of villains.

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:47.900
That's just an idea though, whatever happens
I'll be covering everything Saw here on the

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:48.900
channel.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.260
Starting in March I'm going to be doing Things
You Missed episodes for all the Saw movies

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:55.269
including Spiral, and Horror History episodes
on all your favorite Saw characters, so let

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:58.260
me know who you'd like to see me cover in
the comments, and also these shirts will be

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.989
available in the merch store soon, so make
sure you don't miss out on any of that content

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:06.950
by subscribing to CZsWorld for new horrors
every week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.260
and I'll see you in the next one.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.949
Assuming we both survive.

